{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel journeyed from Beeroth Benei Jaakan to Moserah.</b> What is this passage doing here? And moreover — did they journey from Beeroth Benei Jaakan to Moserah? Was it not from Moserah that they came to Benei Jaakan, as it says ״וַיִּסְעוּ מִמֹּסֵרוֹת וְגוֹ״ (Numbers 33)? And furthermore — there Aaron died, but did he not die at Hor haHar? Go and count and you will find eight stations from Moseroth to Hor haHar! Rather, this too is part of the rebuke: this too you did — when Aaron died at Hor haHar at the end of forty years and the clouds of glory departed, you feared a battle against the king of Arad, and you resolved to turn back to Egypt. You retreated eight stations until Benei Jaakan, and from there to Moserah. There the sons of Levi fought you and killed some of you, and you some of them, until they forced you back on your return path. And from there you returned — Gudgodah, which is Hor haGidgad."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:25.440539587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}